<title>PHILIPPINES: Globe Telecom sees net loss down in 1997.</title>
<headline>Globe Telecom sees net loss down in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Globe Telecom GMCR, a joint venutre between Ayala Corp and Singapore Telecom, forecast on Monday it would post a net loss of 321.2 million pesos in 1997.</p>
<p>It told the Manila Stock Exchange in a disclosure statement that revenues in 1997 were forecast at 2.899 billion pesos.</p>
<p>The company earlier announced it had posted a net loss of 750.9 million pesos in 1996 on revenues of 1.465 billion pesos.</p>
</text>
